Complexity Type	Definition	Average Effort  (PD)
Simple	
"1.	Simple request and response schema (8-10 fields)
2. Simple business validations(1) with only one data entity lookup.
3. Simple transformation with direct object to object mapping with same format
4. Simple Get and Delete operations
5. Integration with one or two tables of the Database
6. Includes simple business logic/computation or NA
7. Auditing & Event Publishing (1 or 2 fields) or NA"	
Effort: 6

Medium	
"1. Request and response schema (20-25 fields), schemas can have nested objects.
2. Complex business validations (2-3) with multiple data entities lookup.
3. Data transformation with direct/indirect mapping, Calling external services/libraries
4. Action routing & Attribute routing
5. All HTTP operations
5. Integration with two or three tables of the Database
6. Includes simple business logic/computation 
7. Auditing & Event Publishing (5 or more fields)"	
Effort: 10

Complex	
"1. Request and response schema (20-30 fields), schemas can have nested objects.
2. Complex business validations (4-5) with multiple data entities lookup.
3. Data transformation with direct/indirect mapping, Calling external services/libraries
4. Orchestrating multiple api calls and fetching the data from multiple sources and returning aggregated response or interacting with 3 to 5 tables in DB and aggregating response
5. Asynchronus pattern, Entity Framework, Unit Of Work
6. Basic authentication, Forms, SSL, Oauth 2.0
7. All HTTP operations
8. Has complex business logic/computation"
Effort: 14

High Complex	
"1.	Request and response schema (50+ fields), schemas can have nested objects.
2. Complex business validations (7+) with multiple data entities lookup.
3. Data transformation with direct/indirect mapping, Calling multiple external services/libraries
4. Orchestrating multiple api calls and fetching the data from multiple sources and returning aggregated response. or interacting with more than 5 tables in DB and aggregating response.
5. Basic authentication, Forms, SSL, Oauth 2.0 & External authentication
6. Advanced patterns such as Entity Framework, Unity Of Work, Generic Repository, DI & IOC, Unity Container & Odata
7. Data encryption & decryption logic
8. All HTTP operations
9. Has very complex business logic/computation"	
Effort: 18
